      },
      "lineNbr": 1094,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T19:44:16Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Now that this is being called by something other than CRAS, I think we need to move `sco_offload` into a getter/setter instead of taking it per `start_sco_call`.\n\nWe don\u0027t expect to simultaneously offload AND inband SCO so it doesn\u0027t make sense to do it per call.\n\n@enshuo@google.com - Thoughts?",
      "revId": "fee10c148ef666e11043a8eba16f7ad149b0955a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "77d52cc6_75db734a",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1094,
      "author": {
        "id": 1543626
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-10T22:57:05Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "To clarify, what\u0027s we want to get by moving the `sco_offload` into a getter/setter? also, is this only about the implementation in bluetooth_media or also for the interface exposed to CRAS? The later may complicates the synchronization between audio and bluetooth stack that I\u0027m not certain if necessary.",
      "parentUuid": "af5f2d3f_618cb90f",
      "revId": "fee10c148ef666e11043a8eba16f7ad149b0955a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "0efde511_4533c4d4",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1094,
      "author": {
        "id": 1836438
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-15T04:59:42Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I don\u0027t think you want per stream control of sco offload. It\u0027s usually something you decide on a per platform level so it belongs as a getter/setter api you call during setup.",
      "parentUuid": "77d52cc6_75db734a",
      "revId": "fee10c148ef666e11043a8eba16f7ad149b0955a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "5721b98f_cd4169e8",
        "filename": "system/gd/rust/linux/stack/src/bluetooth_media.rs",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 1094,
      "author": {
        "id": 1543626
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-02-16T02:04:04Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "No, we don\u0027t.\n\nI didn\u0027t get the point why we want to add the getter/setter interface. Is this to prevent caller calling `start_sco_call` with different `sco_offload` arugment? If yes, we\u0027ll still need to cover the ambiguous case even with the `getter/setter` interface when the setter is called with an active sco call started.\n\nAlso, with the interface changes, It\u0027s not clear to the client that when should it calls the setter, and we\u0027ll need extra effort to deal with the sychronization of `sco_offload` between two stacks.\n\nI\u0027d suggest to merge this first to unblock the qualification and refine the implementation if needed.",
      "parentUuid": "0efde511_4533c4d4",
      "revId": "fee10c148ef666e11043a8eba16f7ad149b0955a",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
